1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,200
8 AM. Three customers at once.
And the khata? That same torn register.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,200
Now just… speak.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:12,000
"2 kilo cheeni, 1 Maggi,
500 gram dal, Ramesh ke naam"

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The bill writes itself —
real voice, real speech-to-text.

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,400
Rs 174. Ramesh. Done.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The customer gets the same bill
on their phone — confirm or dispute.

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,000
New item? The app asks back —
it doesn't guess.

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:40,500
Cash, UPI QR (self-reported),
or khata. Stock updates too.

9
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:47,500
Customer scans the QR,
their own khata opens.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Asking for money is awkward?
The app reminds — politely, by voice.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Milk shop or kirana — deliveries,
leave, accounts. Staff runs it, you watch.

12
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:10,000
Hinglish, Telugu, English.
Like your own shop.

13
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:16,000
Tested in noise. Results public —
failures too.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Bolo. Khata likh gaya.
Bolo Khata — voice-first ledger for dukaans.
